  {
    "title": "Dunge",
    "languages": ["Java (Processing)","XML","JSON"],
    "image": "resources/dunge1.png",
    "desc":
    "
    Dunge is a dungeon crawler & my pet project, I have been working on this game since i was 15.\n\n

    It's my primary source of learning novel concepts in game development.
    ",
    "popup":
    [
        "DUNGE",
        "Infinite dungeon crawler",
        {
        "type": "text",
        "data": ["What is Dunge?",
        "<p>
        Dunge is an infinite dungeon crawler I am always working on, I use it mostly to learn from.\n\n

        Whenever i think of a cool game concept i try to work it out and make it work with all other concepts in this game.
        </p>"]
        },
        {
        "type": "images",
        "data": ["resources/dunge3.png","resources/dunge4.png","resources/dunge5.png"]
        },
        {
        "type": "text",
        "data": ["Features in dunge",
        "<p>
        The game includes:\n
        - Configurable world gen\n
        - XML Based gui\n
        - An animation DSL\n
        - An enemy AI VM-like system (also using a DSL)\n\n

        It's important to note i go into more depth in <a href='https://www.isomeone.nl/dev_docs/dunge'>this document</a>\n
        The GitHub repo is not public, you can E-Mail me for the code.
        </p>"]
        },
        {
        "type": "text",
        "data": ["Languages used",
        "<p>
        I used 2 official languages (Java, XML and JSON), counting the DSLs I used 4.
        </p>"]
        },
        {
        "type": "text",
        "data": ["Older versions",
        "<p>
        In older versions (made in scratch) everything was configurable via JSON, and i made an editor for the animations (in scratch too) see below
        </p>"]
        },
        {
        "type": "image",
        "data": ["resources/dunge6.png"]
        }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "KolomKamers [in dev]",
    "languages": ["JS","Python","HTML","CSS"],
    "image": "resources/kkt.png",
    "desc":
    "
    KolomKamers is an online website creator/editor based on a single central column, Inspired by most of my websites.\n\n

    It has a simple dashboard, drag and drop elements, currently working on api support.
    ",
    "popup":
    [
        "KolomKamers",
        "Online web editor",
        {
        "type": "text",
        "data": ["What is Kolomkamers?",
        "<p>
        Kolomkamers is an easy way to create your own website, You can log in, create a website, and share it with others.\n\n

        It could be used for a simple profile / portfolio or for a document or presentation.
        </p>"]
        },
        {
        "type": "image",
        "data": ["resources/kk1.png"]
        },
        {
        "type": "text",
        "data": ["Features in kolomkamers",
        "<p>
        Up until now it has:\n
        - Login / Signup screen\n
        - Working backend server\n
        - Web Editor\n
        - Compact markup language to save space on server\n\n

        I'm planning to add:\n
        - Style editor (markup language already includes style)\n
        - Custom community made tiles\n
        - API support, allowing users to upload tokens that are kept on my server without being public\n\n

        I'm currently creating a document for this project that goes into more depth, which I will share here when done\n
        The github repo is public <a href='https://github.com/FlorisTim/kolomkamer'>right here</a>
        </p>"]
        },
        {
        "type": "text",
        "data": ["Languages used",
        "<p>
        I used JS and Python for the backend, and html and css if you count those.
        </p>"]
        },
        {
        "type": "image",
        "data": ["resources/kk2.png"]
        }
    ]
